  "intro": {
    "cards": [
      {
        "title": "Subject–verb agreement",
        "title_cz": "Shoda podmětu se slovesem",
        "text_first": true,
        "points": [
          "The verb **fits** the subject: **he works**, **they work**.",
          "You already know this in positives.",
          "The same fit is in questions, **was / were**, and **everybody**.",
          "Czech often uses one form. English does not."
        ],
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Subject",
            "Verb"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "he / she / it",
              "**works** · **was** · **Does he** work?"
            ],
            [
              "they / we / you",
              "**work** · **were** · **Do they** work?"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "do / does",
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Subject",
            "Question / negative"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "I / you / we / they",
              "Do they work? · They don't work."
            ],
            [
              "he / she / it",
              "Does he work? · She doesn't work."
            ]
          ]
        },
        "points": [
          "After do/does, use the **base** verb: Does he **work**? (not works)",
          "Avoid: *Do he work?* · *She don't like…*"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "was / were · there is / are",
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Use",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "**was**",
              "He **was** late. · There **was** a problem."
            ],
            [
              "**were**",
              "They **were** late. · You **were** late. · There **were** problems."
            ],
            [
              "**is** / **are**",
              "There **is** a book. · There **are** two books."
            ]
          ]
        },
        "points": [
          "we → **were** (not was) · you → **were** (not was)",
          "there **is** + singular · there **are** + plural"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "everybody / someone / nobody",
        "points": [
          "**everybody / someone / nobody / everything / each / one of…** take a **singular** verb.",
          "They look like a group. The verb stays singular."
        ],
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Not",
            "Say"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "~~Everybody like weekends.~~",
              "Everybody **likes** weekends."
            ],
            [
              "~~Someone have my keys.~~",
              "Someone **has** my keys."
            ],
            [
              "~~Do everybody understand?~~",
              "**Does** everybody understand?"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Quick check",
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "",
            ""
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "____ he work here?",
              "**Does**"
            ],
            [
              "They ____ like fish.",
              "**don't**"
            ],
            [
              "There ____ two books now.",
              "**are**"
            ],
            [
              "Everybody ____ weekends.",
              "**likes**"
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
